---
Add cJSON NULL checks in project_save.

cJSON creation functions (cJSON_CreateObject, cJSON_CreateArray, etc.)
can return NULL on allocation failure. Current save code doesn't check,
leading to NULL pointer dereference crashes.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Every cJSON_Create* call checked for NULL return
- [ ] On NULL: clean up partially built JSON tree, return error
- [ ] LOG_ERROR on allocation failure
- [ ] Save function returns error code (not void) on failure

## Test Plan
- [ ] Audit all cJSON calls in project_save
- [ ] Verify each has NULL check
- [ ] Optional: inject allocation failure, verify graceful error
